cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "MIZAN kit: statistics, dataset auditing and hardware harnesses for robot learning"
message: "If you use this software or its dataset audit results, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Tarek
    family-names: Okasha
repository-code: "https://github.com/tarekokasha22/mizan-kit"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.2.0
date-released: "2026-09-09"
keywords:
  - robotics
  - robot learning
  - LeRobot
  - dataset quality
  - anytime-valid inference
  - confidence sequences
abstract: >-
  Three components of the MIZAN research programme. cairo_protocol provides
  anytime-valid confidence sequences and fixed-n tests so that a robot trial
  is analysed correctly from the first trial onward. ledger is a temporal
  integrity audit for LeRobot datasets on the Hugging Face Hub, run as a two
  tier census that surveys dataset metadata across the whole population and
  runs per frame checks over a seeded random sample, reporting prevalence
  with confidence intervals. lerobot_ur is a Universal Robots e-Series
  follower over RTDE with a simulator based CI gate.
